From 86ac6ae5a351f3ab57c75f48e34968a833756a95 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Arnaud Pouliquen <arnaud.pouliquen@foss.st.com>
Date: Fri, 24 Jul 2026 09:55:13 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] dt-bindings: remoteproc: add post-init-providers property
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

The device can references power domain as provider.

When the node is declared under a ahb bus parent, this one is bound before.
In such case, the fw_devlink “dangling consumer pickup” mechanism
re-attributes rproc fwnode links to the ahb bus fwnode.

Later when the rproc node is probed, a link is created between it
and the power domain, but the link to ahb is not purged, causing this
warning:

genpd_provider power-domain-retention: sync_state() pending due to ahb@2

The post-init-providers property avoid enforcing the sync_state dependency
for this link. The link is created later during rproc probing.

Change-Id: Ib4fcbe763a5136de3a038a76a147d1347375773f
Signed-off-by: Arnaud Pouliquen <arnaud.pouliquen@foss.st.com>
Reviewed-on: https://gerrit.st.com/c/mpu/oe/st/linux-stm32/+/591636
ACI: CIBUILD <MDG-smet-aci-builds@list.st.com>
Domain-Review: Patrick DELAUNAY <patrick.delaunay@foss.st.com>
Reviewed-by: Arnaud POULIQUEN <arnaud.pouliquen@st.com>
Reviewed-by: Olivier MOYSAN <olivier.moysan@foss.st.com>
ACI: CITOOLS <MDG-smet-aci-reviews@list.st.com>
Tested-by: Arnaud POULIQUEN <arnaud.pouliquen@st.com>
---
 .../devicetree/bindings/remoteproc/st,stm32-rproc.yaml          | 2 ++
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+)

diff --git a/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/remoteproc/st,stm32-rproc.yaml b/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/remoteproc/st,stm32-rproc.yaml
index aa63899c1406..456f97902c03 100644
--- a/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/remoteproc/st,stm32-rproc.yaml
+++ b/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/remoteproc/st,stm32-rproc.yaml
@@ -179,6 +179,8 @@ properties:
       - const: default
       - const: sleep
 
+  post-init-providers: true
+
   keep-power-in-suspend:
     $ref: /schemas/types.yaml#/definitions/flag
     description:
